Setting, continuing the previous page. The rotation group G = Aut^+(Cube) is identified with S_I, where I is the 4-element set of main diagonals. J is the 3-element set of face-directions (face axes). Each i in J is a partition Q_i of I into two pairs. D_i = I/Q_i is the corresponding 2-element set, an F_2-torsor. V is the Klein four-group of 'translations' (the rotations by pi about the face axes).

First two lines (end of an argument). The map I -> prod_{i in J} D_i, sending a diagonal to the pair containing it in each partition, is injective. Its image is a torsor under V_J(F_2) = {xi in F_2^J : sum xi_i = 0}, sitting inside the F_2^J-torsor prod D_i. This is a reduction of the structure group from F_2^J to V_J(F_2). Hence the contracted (Baer) product of the F_2-torsors is trivial: wedge_{i in J} D_i ≅ 1. Grothendieck marks this 'OK'. It is the combinatorial F_2-shadow of the formula wedge_{i in J} M_i = 0 proved on the next page for free Z/4-modules M of rank 2. That page in fact develops the general M_0-torsor version.

Main body. Grothendieck proposes to interpret the 10 isomorphism classes of homogeneous G-spaces with isotropy ≠ G, i.e. the conjugacy classes of proper subgroups of S_4, as natural 'elements of structure' of the cube.

The seven he lists first:
- vertices (8, stabilizer C3);
- edges (12, stabilizer generated by a transposition);
- faces (6, C4);
- antipodal pairs of vertices = main diagonals = I (4, S3);
- antipodal pairs of edges (6, the non-normal Klein group);
- antipodal pairs of faces = J (3, D4);
- frames / repères of the axes (24, trivial stabilizer).

The remaining three:
- A set of cardinality 2: a quotient of the vertex set, namely the two inscribed tetrahedra, i.e. the orientations; stabilizer A4. The margin note describes it via the parity of distance between vertices.
- The 12 face diagonals: stabilizer generated by a double transposition, i.e. an element of order 2 of V.
- The 6-element set G/V ≅ S_3 = Aut(J): interpreted as the set of ordered pairs of distinct elements of J, i.e. 'frames' of J, with J read as the directions of faces (equivalently of edges).

'Le compte y est !' The cardinalities 24, 12, 12, 8, 6, 6, 6, 4, 3, 2 are exactly the indices of the 10 classes of proper subgroups of S_4.

Purpose. This is a dictionary for level-4 structures. PSL_2(Z/4) ≅ S_4 is the octahedral group, X(4) is the cube/octahedron 'regular map', and the intermediate quotients are the level-4 modular curves. It prepares Section 5 (free rank-2 modules over Z/4, torsors M_i, P_M).
